From 072bb5a4dedd2e28a4460cf3a478adf21fddf2e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:08:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 62/69] Support cartridge banks 0 through 254

Region masks and fixed cartridge arrays limited placement to 64 banks.
Unchecked pragma shifts could silently alias higher banks to lower ones;
the frozen compiler maps bank 64 to bank 0 on this host.

Use a four-word CartridgeBankSet and allocate bank images on demand.
Validate region and overlay banks before narrowing, preserve 255 as the
__bankof sentinel, and update placement, relocation, listings and outputs.
Write high EasyFlash banks with a single post-processing warning and
encode CHIP bank fields with flip16. Preserve zero-filled unused NES banks.

Build and full autotest pass: 1531 emulations versus the baseline's 1521,
with no new failures. Add coverage for high banks and the __bankof sentinel,
registered in the batch driver like the other tests.
Check CRT packets, PRG/D64 overlays, invalid banks, shared banks, overlap
checks and NES images. Across 27 regression cases, binaries, maps and
labels match exactly; listing differences are only absolute include paths.
Three sprite samples fail identically in both compilers.

Written by Codex; checked by Claude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
